cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it as below. A Zenodo DOI is minted per release; once the first DOI exists it is added here under 'identifiers'."
type: dataset
title: "gp-omm-conformance: a conformance corpus for orbital-data parsers crossing the five-digit catalog-number boundary (Alpha-5, six- and nine-digit NORAD_CAT_IDs, CCSDS OMM)"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: Honorius
    family-names: Neogy
    affiliation: "NEOGY LLC"
    # role: author and maintainer; copyright holder is NEOGY LLC
repository-code: "https://github.com/hneogy/gp-omm-conformance"
abstract: >-
  Expected values, structural checks, specification vectors, derived Alpha-5 TLE lines and a
  standard-library runner that test whether an orbital-data parser handles the 2026 migration of
  the US satellite catalog past five-digit numbers: Alpha-5 encoding, six- and nine-digit catalog
  numbers, and the CCSDS Orbit Mean-Elements Message in CSV, JSON, XML and KVN as served by
  CelesTrak. Raw provider data is not redistributed; a fetch script rebuilds it locally under the
  provider's terms and SHA-256 hashes identify the tested snapshot. Built with AI assistance under
  human direction, independently audited before release (AUDIT.md), decision log in DECISIONS.md.
keywords:
  - satellite catalog
  - two-line element set
  - Alpha-5
  - OMM
  - CCSDS 502.0-B-3
  - SGP4
  - CelesTrak
  - conformance testing
